| MAJOR | Scope Boundaries: “scheduler status should avoid work not required for status registration if feasible”; Files: `src/worldenergydata/scheduler/cli.py`, `src/worldenergydata/scheduler/scheduler.py` | The plan does not define how `status` can list seven jobs without importing job classes, while preserving `cmd_status(jobs=...)`, `cmd_run_job`, `start`, config-derived `next_run`, and existing scheduler tests. A vague “lazy metadata registry” can easily break runtime job execution or status completeness. | Specify the lazy design before implementation: job metadata/name registry for `status`, factory registry for `run-job`/`start`, and compatibility rules for injected `jobs` in tests/API. |
